That's false, because rabbis are intellectuals.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
That's right.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.000
No, I'm sorry.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.000
It's a difference between a hakam and an intellectual.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.000
A hakam is somebody who knows.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.000
Learned.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.000
Learned.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.000
Learned.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:24.000
Once I went to a friend of mine, I had to borrow a Hebrew book from somebody.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.000
That was a year or two ago.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.000
I had a Hebrew book.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.000
That was a very anti-intellectual statement.

